Z||000000||d825077||11-23-2000||07:41 PM||||I checked my air filter today and noticed the gasket between the motor and air filter container was dry rotted.  I have a 1984 4 cylinder automatic.  Can I buy the gasket at Pepboys, or is it a dealer part?  Does anyone know what it is called so I can ask for it by name?<P>thank you||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||08:06 PM||||Felpro part # 60797. I couldn't get it at Autozone, but they were kind enough to give me the part #.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||bHooper||11-23-2000||08:22 PM||||hey, rock, is that the part number for the 6 cyl cars?  i believe the feller was looking for the one that fits 4 bangers.<P>but thanks for the part number!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">   <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||4
Z||000003||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||09:42 PM||||Yeah, I know he was asking about a four cyl, but I screwed up anyway. The correct # is 60535 for the air cleaner gasket, and 60536 for the T/B to manifold gasket. The # I gave above is a T/B to manifold gasket for a GM crossfire which I had on the same Autozone receipt. Sorry for any confusion.||||reg||1
Z||000004||horseman||11-24-2000||10:53 PM||||Just go to a good speed shop and ask for an air breather to throttle body assy. gasket. Heck, it only takes 30 sec. to remove it so take it with you. Average cost is less than two bucks. If you go to autozone or pepboys you might confuse one of the ex burger boys.Make sure you tell them the correct spelling of F-I-E-R-O. They can't do anything without the computer. <P>Charlie||||reg||1
